<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-24T06:37:45+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sat, 24 Oct 2026 06:37:45 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[After Operation Sindoor friction, Delhi &amp; Baku reset ties with EAM Jaishankar's visit]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135155334.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Ties between the two countries had been held back by geopolitical reasons for a while, mainly Azerbaijan’s ties with Pakistan — as evident from its support for Islamabad after Op Sindoor last year — and India’s defence ties with Armenia. While Bayramov spoke about taking the relationship to a higher level, setting aside past differences, Jaishankar underlined the significance of trade and energy cooperation. Terrorism was also discussed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/after-operation-sindoor-friction-delhi-baku-reset-ties-with-eam-jaishankars-visit/articleshow/135155334.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:36:48+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155369,imgsize-48706.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Study traces how an El Niño changed the pollution map]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154890.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Coming ahead of India’s peak pollution season, the paper, titled ‘Air quality in flux: The baffling ENSO transition in India’, published in Atmospheric Pollution Research journal Thursday, found that La Niña/El Niño conditions altered atmospheric circulation, PM2.5 transport pathways and weather conditions that determine whether pollution disperses or gets trapped.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/study-traces-how-an-el-nio-changed-the-pollution-map/articleshow/135154890.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:32:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amitava Bhattacharya</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155262,imgsize-1950721.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cabinet secretariat merely acknowledged complaint of ECs against senior poll officer: RTI]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154891.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Explaining the rationale behind the reluctance to take any action, a confidential note on the file shared by the Cabinet secretariat with transparency activist, Commodore Lokesh K Batra (Retd), as part of its 21-page RTI reply, stated that EC being a Constitutional body is insulated from the Executive's interference by design.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cabinet-secretariat-merely-acknowledged-complaint-of-ecs-against-senior-poll-officer-rti/articleshow/135154891.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:28:41+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155199,imgsize-309298.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China’s patrolling deviations disturb border: MEA on ITBP DG's LAC face-offs remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135155021.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The ministry of external affairs (MEA) on Friday did not go into the specifics of the latest face-off, choosing to refer the issue to the defence ministry, but said Chinese divergence from established patrolling patterns created disturbances at the border from time to time. The official said both sides continued to use existing diplomatic and military mechanisms to resolve outstanding issues and avoid misunderstanding and miscalculation along the LAC.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/chinas-patrolling-deviations-disturb-border-mea-on-itbp-dgs-lac-face-offs-remark/articleshow/135155021.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:25:14+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155098,imgsize-45698.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Northwest India turned drier, south wetter over 70 years, finds IMD study]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154893.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In northwest India, the hot semi-arid zone grew from about a quarter of the region’s area in 1951-1980 to a third in 1991-2020, while the temperate zone shrank from about a quarter to less than a fifth, meaning that an area equal to roughly 7% of the region moved into the drier zone as temperatures rose and rainfall declined, said the study.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/northwest-india-turned-drier-south-wetter-over-70-years-finds-imd-study/articleshow/135154893.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T01:24:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishwa Mohan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135155143,imgsize-294286.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arms training case: US mercenary VanDyke, 6 Ukrainians to remain abroad till Feb 24]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154247.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[VanDyke attended the court hearing Friday and sought the release of his seized personal articles. The seven accused had earlier sought six weeks to meet their families and were allowed to stay abroad till Oct 23. They were arrested on March 13 for allegedly training the insurgent-linked groups in Myanmar.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/arms-training-case-us-mercenary-vandyke-6-ukrainians-to-remain-abroad-till-feb-24/articleshow/135154247.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:50:07+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154643,imgsize-37086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Opposition's 'mock Parliament' to step up fight against SIR &amp; CEC Gyanesh Kumar]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154248.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sources said a “mock” gathering depicting an assembly of MPs may take place in the national capital on Oct 28. The event will involve MPs and others, but is unlikely to be a large gathering, given that a massive show of strength to push for the CEC’s resignation is planned at Ramlila Maidan as a “Delhi chalo” rally.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/oppositions-mock-parliament-to-step-up-fight-against-sir-cec-gyanesh-kumar/articleshow/135154248.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:45:37+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154589,imgsize-160956.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Need to unite against divisive forces, tackle new challenges: PM Modi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154250.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Inaugurating the Chinmaya Amrit Mahotsav Global Sammelan, he said Swami Chinmayananda set his goals as per issues facing the country at the time and new challenges had emerged in the past few decades. “We must unite society against divisive forces. We must inspire citizens toward self-reliance, and we must connect every individual to vision of a developed India by 2047. For these objectives, we must become more proactive,” he said.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/need-to-unite-against-divisive-forces-tackle-new-challenges-pm-modi/articleshow/135154250.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:42:30+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154532,imgsize-67060.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre bans reuse of single-use medical devices across hospitals; flags recycling of disposables]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154254.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a letter dated Oct 16, the Directorate General of Health Services (DGHS) said it had come to its notice that some private and corporate hospitals were reusing single-use devices after sterilising them, including items used in cardiology, nephrology, oncology, cardiothoracic and vascular surgery (CTVS), neurosurgery and other clinical services. The DGHS said that reuse could expose patients to cross-infection, device malfunction, reduced performance and other complications.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-bans-reuse-of-single-use-medical-devices-across-hospitals-flags-recycling-of-disposables/articleshow/135154254.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:37:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154373,imgsize-175138.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Brics parliamentary meet should end with joint statement: Lok Sabha Speaker Om Birla]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/brics-parliamentary-meet-should-end-with-joint-statement-lok-sabha-speaker-om-birla/articleshow/135154253.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135154253.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Talking to reporters Friday, Birla said the forum in India would work towards consensus-based dialogue on the role of Parliament in strengthening institutions, promotion of human-centred innovation in AI and digital technologies through Parliament, more representative system of global governance and role of Parliament in ensuring a sustainable and inclusive future for Brics countries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/brics-parliamentary-meet-should-end-with-joint-statement-lok-sabha-speaker-om-birla/articleshow/135154253.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/brics-parliamentary-meet-should-end-with-joint-statement-lok-sabha-speaker-om-birla/articleshow/135154253.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-24T00:37:06+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135154451,imgsize-195304.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Parl panel bats for intercensal surveys, gender-inclusive census town norms]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/parl-panel-bats-for-intercensal-surveys-gender-inclusive-census-town-norms/articleshow/135152492.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135152492.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/parl-panel-bats-for-intercensal-surveys-gender-inclusive-census-town-norms/articleshow/135152492.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/parl-panel-bats-for-intercensal-surveys-gender-inclusive-census-town-norms/articleshow/135152492.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T23:16:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135152503,imgsize-142074.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Gurjar Mahasabha flags lack of political representation, seeks greater share in legislatures, institutions]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gurjar-mahasabha-flags-lack-of-political-representation-seeks-greater-share-in-legislatures-institutions/articleshow/135151131.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135151131.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Scheduled for October 27, the Akhil Bharatiya Gurjar Mahasabha's national convention aims to tackle pressing representation issues faced by the Gurjar community, evidenced by just 20 MLAs in a pool of approximately 4,600 across India. Key demands include the formation of a Gurjar Regiment and reserved positions, as well as initiatives focused on youth development and substance abuse awareness.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gurjar-mahasabha-flags-lack-of-political-representation-seeks-greater-share-in-legislatures-institutions/articleshow/135151131.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/gurjar-mahasabha-flags-lack-of-political-representation-seeks-greater-share-in-legislatures-institutions/articleshow/135151131.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-23T22:28:52+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135151240,imgsize-125944.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Jamia protest: Congress MP Imran Masood detained, SP MP alleges manhandling by police]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jamia-protest-congress-mp-imran-masood-detained-sp-mp-alleges-manhandling-by-police/articleshow/135150459.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135150459.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/jamia-protest-congress-mp-imran-masood-d